1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
So I have a friend.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
She's an actress. She's in her 60s.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
And a couple of days before Christmas,

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
she was at the post office.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Out of nowhere, someone moved her out of the way.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Just physically put their hands on her

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,830
and moved her out of the way.

8
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:20,830
He apparently needed something that she was blocking.

9
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:21,830
So he moved her.

10
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:24,860
She said that she was shocked at first.

11
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:25,860
Yeah.

12
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:29,990
And then a fury rose up in her that she could not explain.

13
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:31,990
Not annoyance.

14
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,990
Not frustration.

15
00:00:33,990 --> 00:00:36,990
But fury was the word that she used.

16
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:38,990
And she went on to say,

17
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:40,990
I don't know. I was furious.

18
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:42,990
And I don't know why.

19
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:43,990
I mean, he didn't hit me.

20
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,990
He didn't hurt me. He didn't violate me.

21
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:48,990
He moved me.

22
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:51,990
There's a culture of men helping themselves to women.

23
00:00:51,990 --> 00:00:54,990
And in this case, in a seemingly innocuous way.

24
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:58,990
But the innocuous makes space for the horrific.

25
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:04,500
And women have to live with the effects of both

26
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,920
and everything in between.

27
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,920
When someone helps themselves to a woman,

28
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:15,920
it not only triggers discomfort and distress,

29
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,950
but the unspoken experiences of our mother's lives,

30
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:25,950
sister's lives, and generations of women before us.

31
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:31,100
That's lifetimes of women dealing with men

32
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:36,360
who assume they know better for us than we know for ourselves.

33
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:40,360
Women have been trained to think that we are overreacting

34
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:44,360
or that we're being too sensitive or unreasonable.

35
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:46,360
We try to make sense of nonsense,

36
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,360
and we swallow the furious feelings.

37
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:51,360
We try to put them into some hidden place in our minds,

38
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:53,360
but they don't go away.

39
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:57,540
That fury sits deep inside

40
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:00,540
as we practice our smiles.

41
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:02,540
Yes, of course.

42
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,540
And try to be pleasant.

43
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,570
Yes, of course.

44
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:10,570
Because apparently women aren't supposed to get angry.

45
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:13,820
When someone thinks they can help themselves to our bodies,

46
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:17,820
it not only ignites the current fury,

47
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,820
but it lights up the past.

48
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:24,300
Today, the global collection of women's experiences

49
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,300
can no longer be ignored.

50
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,820
Times up on thinking that we're overreacting,

51
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,520
or this is just the way it is.

52
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:39,520
Times up on women being held responsible for men's bad behavior.

53
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:45,520
It is men's responsibility to change men's bad behavior.

54
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:52,540
And women, I encourage you to acknowledge your fury.

55
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:55,440
Give it language.

56
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,860
Your fury is not something to be afraid of.

57
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:03,180
It holds lifetimes of wisdom.

58
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:08,260
Let it breathe and listen.

